WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.120
 Oh, I'm getting overwhelmed.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.350
I can't start crying
before the movie starts.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:06.150
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:08.760
CO-HOST: The world premiere
of Marvel Studios' Eternals

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:09.600
was epic.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:10.800
 And if you missed
a moment of it,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.110
don't worry, because you
can catch it all right here,

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.820
presented by Lexus.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:18.400
CO-HOST: We are
live in Hollywood.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.860
 That's the biggest
carpet I've been on.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:20.660
 Gilgamesh.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:21.460
Gilgamesh.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.260
 Gilgamesh.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.380
Gilgamesh.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.160
 I like to call him the
revolutionary evolutionary.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.360
CO-HOST: Speak on it.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.570
 How do you prepare for a
role where you're shooting

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:29.800
cosmic beams out of your eyes?

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:30.820
Like, I don't know.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:34.120
 A lot of staring in the mirror
and practicing your laser eyes.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.430
 Did you do any
actual research on set,

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:37.690
maybe take some things home?

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:39.430
We won't tell
anybody, I promise.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:42.100
We won't tell Kevin.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.300
INTERPRETER: Oh,
what if I tell you?

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.410
No, no, no.
I can't tell you.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.210
No.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.350
 We know you have a couple
brothers and a couple siblings,

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.720
what was their reaction
when you found out?

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:52.100
 They didn't really think
I was going to get it.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:55.430
 I'm sure everybody says this
when they do a movie together,

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:56.815
but we really became a family.

00:00:56.815 --> 00:00:58.970
[LAUGHTER]

00:00:58.970 --> 00:00:59.870
 MCU.
Anything can happen.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:00.670
 Well, there we go.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:01.760
Anything can happen.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.129
 So yeah, it's going to be
a different relationship.

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:04.929
And--

00:01:04.929 --> 00:01:06.480
 They told me to
crash this party.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:07.330
 Oh, they told you?

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:08.530
 Somebody told me
crash your party.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:09.860
 Who told you?

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:10.800
 But how do you--

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.070
you know, with you
and Richard Madden,

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:14.200
how did you go about
creating this relationship

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.500
that spans thousands of years
and has that rich history?

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:18.940
 We know how to push
each other's buttons.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:20.590
We know how to make
each other laugh.

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:23.560
We can infuriate each other
as well at times, so kind of

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:26.710
like, yeah, an old married
couple in many ways.

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:28.240
 Here we were, finishing
the Infinity saga,

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.640
and I was thinking, where
do we go from here, how do

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:32.470
we continue, where do we grow?

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.720
And Chloe came in and told us.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.850
 I'm in awe of that woman.

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:40.330
And it was exciting to
come to work every day

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:43.750
and just to watch her and
be a part of her mind,

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:45.760
because you become
a part of her mind.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.780
Guys, look at the moon.

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:49.190
That's so beautiful.
Sorry.

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:50.530
 You have no idea
how much I love her.

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:52.050
- Look at the moon, Victoria.
- How much I love this man.

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.480
- Look at at the moon.
- How much I love this--

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.070
 You can't fly in real life?

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:55.870
 Not in real life.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:57.370
Don't tell my
nephews and my niece.

00:01:57.370 --> 00:01:58.960
 What was the hardest
part about keeping

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:01.030
everything secret?

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:03.250
 Calling up all my
enemies and telling them

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:04.310
I'm in a Marvel movie.

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:05.110
I don't enemies.

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:06.040
CO-HOST: Look at me now.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:07.497
 Yeah.

00:02:07.497 --> 00:02:08.830
 It was really fun,
because I got to do

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:09.763
a lot of hand choreography.

00:02:09.763 --> 00:02:10.930
I don't want to
give anything away.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.940
I don't want to
get killed, but--

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:14.980
 I know a bunch of stuff.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:16.610
Guys, I know a lot of stuff.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:17.480
I'm not joking.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:20.560
 I heard you say once that
this was kind of a coming of age

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.560
story for Sersi, which I think
is so interesting, because, you

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:26.840
know, 7,000 years old, you
think she's already here,

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.820
but talk to us a
little bit more about--

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:29.620
 I know.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.270
You'd have thought,
after 7,000 years,

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:33.340
she would have-- no, it
turns out there are still

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.660
some things for her to learn.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.580
 What I love about being
a part of this universe is

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:40.000
the diversity and the inclusion,
and so people can recognize

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.130
that people who look
like you are out here--

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:44.350
people who may be
different sizes,

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.540
who love differently, who are--

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:47.510
all are inclusive.

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:50.920
So it's really great to show
that anybody can be a hero.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.540
 Well, we want to ask
you more questions,

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.255
but clearly you only
know that you're

00:02:54.255 --> 00:02:55.255
a guy who works in the museum.

00:02:55.255 --> 00:02:57.260
 A guy who works in the museum.
That's what I'm running with.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:57.910
 There's nothing
more to ask there.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:58.150
Great.

00:02:58.150 --> 00:02:59.183
 That's what I'm running with.

00:02:59.183 --> 00:03:01.510
 I can't wait to see Dane
working in the museum.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.610
That's what I came here for,
and that's what they did too.

